Critical Constraints

1. Do not guess the RT agent endpoint or request schema.
2. Inspect both repositories before making changes.
3. Do not hardcode environment-specific URLs or credentials.
4. Do not expose secrets in browser code.
5. Use the existing UI API/client architecture.
6. Use the existing RT agent API and LangGraph architecture.
7. Preserve streaming behavior if it already exists.
8. Preserve authentication and security requirements.
9. Do not duplicate existing schemas or clients unnecessarily.
10. Keep the UI decoupled from RT agent implementation details.
11. Use existing logging, tracing, retry, and error-handling patterns.
12. Add tests for the complete handshake.
13. Do not modify business logic unrelated to the UI-to-agent integration.
14. Keep the integration extensible for future agent capabilities.

